      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Dalsinghsarai Safe</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Transporting a two-wheeler to Dalsinghsarai requires meticulous preparation to ensure regulatory compliance and asset safety. Before dispatching your bike, you must gather specific documentation that serves as the legal backbone of the transit process. The most critical document is the Registration Certificate (RC).</p>
<p>You must provide a self-attested photocopy of this document. This copy must be clear and legible, as it verifies ownership and is required by transport authorities at every checkpoint. Ensure that the self-attestation includes your signature and the current date to meet legal standards.</p>
<p>In addition to ownership proof, the vehicle must be legally fit for road transport. This necessitates a current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate. An expired PUC certificate can lead to immediate confiscation of the vehicle at transit stations, causing significant delays and potential fines. Therefore, verify the validity date before booking your transport slot.</p>
<p>Equally important is a valid insurance certificate. This document proves that the vehicle is insured for third-party liability and accidental damage during the journey. Without active insurance, you remain fully liable for any incidents that may occur while the bike is in transit.</p>
<p>For the logistics aspect, you must possess an IBA-approved consignment bilty. This is the official receipt and contract between you and the logistics provider. It details the contents, weight, and destination of the shipment.</p>
<p>The bilty must be approved by the Indian Business Association or relevant regulatory bodies to ensure the transport agency is legitimate and covered under standard industry protocols. This document is your only legal claim reference if any dispute arises regarding the delivery status or condition of the bike.</p>
<p>Crucially, you must highlight the inclusion of 100% declared-value marine transit insurance. Standard bike transport often only covers third-party liability, which does not protect your personal asset. Marine transit insurance specifically covers the physical vehicle against theft, fire, or accidental damage during the journey.</p>
<p>By opting for 100% declared-value coverage, you ensure that in the event of total loss, the insurer compensates you for the full market value of your bike, as stated in the policy. This level of coverage is essential for high-value motorcycles or customized bikes.</p>
